00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:07,344
Can you show me ServiceAccounts?

2
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:11,209
A ServiceAccount is an identity for a workload:

3
00:00:11,209 --> 00:00:14,940
a Pod that talks to the Kubernetes API (to list Pods,

4
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:19,164
read a ConfigMap, create a Job) does it as a ServiceAccount.

5
00:00:19,164 --> 00:00:23,880
Kubernetes gives the Pod a short-lived token proving that identity.

6
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:24,725
The analogy:

7
00:00:24,725 --> 00:00:32,047
people get a personal badge (a user account); the delivery robot in the building gets its own badge too,

8
00:00:32,047 --> 00:00:36,975
with its own name, so the doors know it is the robot and not a person.

9
00:00:37,533 --> 00:00:40,576
Some applications need the Kubernetes API:

10
00:00:40,576 --> 00:00:44,923
a CI runner creating Pods, a monitoring agent reading nodes,

11
00:00:44,923 --> 00:00:51,153
an operator managing a database, the ingress controller reading Ingresses (lesson 20).

12
00:00:51,153 --> 00:00:57,962
Each needs an identity, so that permissions (lesson 24) can be given to that application only,

13
00:00:57,962 --> 00:01:01,874
and so the audit log shows which application did what.

14
00:01:01,874 --> 00:01:06,511
| | User | ServiceAccount | |---|---|---| | Who | a person (you,

15
00:01:06,511 --> 00:01:12,596
a colleague) | a workload (a Pod) | | Created by | outside Kubernetes (certificates,

16
00:01:12,596 --> 00:01:15,638
an identity provider) | Kubernetes itself:

17
00:01:15,638 --> 00:01:16,001
kind:

18
00:01:16,001 --> 00:01:25,853
ServiceAccount | | Scope | the cluster | one namespace | | Name in permissions | developer | system:serviceaccount:<namespace>:<name> |.

19
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:30,019
And how does it actually work?

20
00:01:30,567 --> 00:01:37,053
Every namespace has a ServiceAccount called default; a Pod that names none uses it.

21
00:01:37,053 --> 00:01:40,491
spec.serviceAccountName chooses another one.

22
00:01:40,491 --> 00:01:54,480
The kubelet mounts a token, the cluster's CA certificate and the namespace into /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/; the token is short-lived and renewed automatically.

23
00:01:54,480 --> 00:02:00,497
The API server is reachable from every Pod at https://kubernetes.default.svc.

24
